<title>PARAGUAY: SOCCER-PARAGUAY BEAT CHILE 2-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-PARAGUAY BEAT CHILE 2-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paraguay beat Chile 2-1 (halftime 1-1) in a South American World Cup qualifying match on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Paraguay - Carlos Gamarra (24th minute), Catalino Rivarola (63rd)</p>
<p>Chile - Javier Margas (22nd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabuluate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Colombia    5  4  1  0 10  3 13</p>
<p> Ecuador     5  3  0  2  8  6  9</p>
<p> Argentina   5  2  2  1  9  6  8</p>
<p> Paraguay    4  2  1  1  5  3  7</p>
<p> Uruguay     4  2  0  2  4  5  6</p>
<p> Bolivia     4  1  1  2  7  5  4</p>
<p> Chile	 4  1  1  2  7  8  4</p>
<p> Peru	  4  0  3  1  2  5  3</p>
<p> Venezuela   5  0  1  4  4 15  1</p>
<p>Note: top four teams qualify for the 1998 World Cup in France. Brazil qualify automatically as holders. matches:</p>
